--- xah lee wrote:
> i haven't learned about KOha, 

{mi}, {do}, {ta} are all members of KOhA, so you have learned
at least some part of it. KOhA contains all the pronouns.

> I, 

If you say more than one sentence, you normally separate them 
with {.i}.

> UI... 

Those are the attitudinals, a very important part of lojban.

> but i know there are bo and (ke, 
> ke'i)... surely lojban isn't complete without these??

ke and ke'e are very rarely used. bo is more often used
in the {i <tag> bo} or the {na'e bo} constructions than
in tanru. In the end it's a matter of taste whether you
think ke-ke'e, bo or co is more essential for lojban.
I wouldn't include bo and ke-ke'e in my minimal lojban,
but that's just my point of view.

